From: Korri RG353M bring-up <noreply@korri.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] allocator: let the caller name the DRM device

MPP opens the first path in its list that opens at all. It never checks
whether the device can serve DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB, so naming the wrong
device is fatal rather than skipped.

/dev/dri/cardN is assigned in driver probe order, not by role. On the RG353M
the display controller (rockchipdrm, display-subsystem) provides the dumb
buffer allocator MPP needs, while the GPU (panfrost, fde60000.gpu) is
render-only and provides none. Loading panfrost from the initrd makes it probe
first, which moves the GPU to card0 and leaves MPP with two unusable entries:
card0 and renderD128 are then both panfrost. Every allocation fails with
"drm_alloc failed ret -1" and the encoder crashes.

Read the device from the mpp_drm_dev environment variable so the caller can
name the display controller by a stable path, and keep the built-in list as
the fallback for callers that set nothing. Reorder that fallback to try card0
before renderD128, since the render node cannot allocate dumb buffers.

---
 osal/allocator/allocator_drm.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/osal/allocator/allocator_drm.c
+++ b/osal/allocator/allocator_drm.c
@@ -58,10 +58,19 @@
     RK_U32  flags;
 } allocator_ctx_drm;
 
-/* use renderD128 first to avoid GKI kernel permission issue */
+/*
+ * The loop below takes the first path that opens and never checks whether the
+ * device can actually serve DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATE_DUMB, so a wrong entry is
+ * fatal rather than skipped. /dev/dri/cardN is assigned in driver probe order,
+ * not by role: on a board where a render-only GPU such as Panfrost probes
+ * first, card0 is the GPU and has no KMS, and every allocation then fails.
+ *
+ * Let the caller name the device through the mpp_drm_dev environment variable
+ * and keep this list only as the fallback for boards that are not configured.
+ */
 static const char *dev_drm[] = {
-    "/dev/dri/renderD128",
     "/dev/dri/card0",
+    "/dev/dri/renderD128",
 };
 
 static RK_U32 to_rockchip_gem_mem_flag(RK_U32 flags)
@@ -158,6 +167,7 @@
 static MPP_RET os_allocator_drm_open(void **ctx, size_t alignment, MppAllocFlagType flags)
 {
     allocator_ctx_drm *p;
+    const char *dev_cfg = NULL;
     RK_S32 fd;
     RK_S32 i;
 
@@ -169,16 +179,30 @@
     *ctx = NULL;
 
     mpp_env_get_u32("drm_debug", &drm_debug, 0);
+    mpp_env_get_str("mpp_drm_dev", &dev_cfg, NULL);
+
+    fd = -1;
+
+    if (dev_cfg) {
+        fd = open(dev_cfg, O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC);
+        if (fd <= 0)
+            mpp_err_f("open configured drm device %s failed: %s\n",
+                      dev_cfg, strerror(errno));
+    }
 
-    for (i = 0; i < (RK_S32)MPP_ARRAY_ELEMS(dev_drm); i++) {
-        fd = open(dev_drm[i], O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC);
-        if (fd > 0)
-            break;
+    if (fd <= 0) {
+        for (i = 0; i < (RK_S32)MPP_ARRAY_ELEMS(dev_drm); i++) {
+            fd = open(dev_drm[i], O_RDWR | O_CLOEXEC);
+            if (fd > 0)
+                break;
+        }
     }
 
     if (fd < 0) {
         mpp_err_f("open all drm device failed.\n");
         mpp_err("Please check the following device path and access permission:\n");
+        if (dev_cfg)
+            mpp_err("%s (from mpp_drm_dev)\n", dev_cfg);
         for (i = 0; i < (RK_S32)MPP_ARRAY_ELEMS(dev_drm); i++)
             mpp_err("%s\n", dev_drm[i]);
         return MPP_ERR_UNKNOW;
